<title>USA: Fed seen staying out of system, but add possible.</title>
<headline>Fed seen staying out of system, but add possible.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve was expected to remain out of the banking system at its usual midmorning intervention period on Tuesday, but there was a chance it would add reserves via term repurchase agreements, economists said.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at 5.44 percent, slightly below the Fed's current official target level of 5.50 percent.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660))</p>
</text>
